  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1232 PM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nThings dry out by Wednesday night with upper level flow becoming \nzonal for the rest of the week. This will keep the weather quiet \nwith highs in the upper 60s to lower 70s. A short wave trough and \npush of cold air will make it to the Great Lakes over the weekend.\nSome of that cold air will make it here and will bring below \nnormal highs with them falling into the lower 60s. Overnight lows \nwill also be cold falling into the 30s and a frost will be likely \nstarting Saturday night. Lows below 32 are also looking likely for\nthe Plateau starting Saturday night. Troughing will continue into\nearly next week with the cold temps sticking around. No precip \nexpected for the extended period.",
